WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.360
In 1665, Robert Hooke cut an exceedingly thin slice of cork.

2
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.920
He saw rows of tiny walled boxes.

3
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.860
He called them cells.

4
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.780
They were walls left by cork cells that had died.

5
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:26.200
About 175 years passed before scientists argued that plants and animals alike are

6
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.140
built of cells. Why did it take so long?

7
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:32.643
The cell theory has six ideas.

8
00:00:33.523 --> 00:00:35.823
All living organisms are made of cells.

9
00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:38.783
Cells are the basic unit of life.

10
00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:42.543
All cells arise from pre-existing cells.

11
00:00:43.523 --> 00:00:48.703
Metabolism, all the chemical reactions in a living thing, happens inside cells.

12
00:00:49.703 --> 00:00:53.763
Hereditary information, called DNA, passes from cell to cell.

13
00:00:54.623 --> 00:00:57.083
All cells have the same basic composition.

14
00:00:58.017 --> 00:01:02.297
Magnification is how many times larger an image looks.

15
00:01:03.477 --> 00:01:07.597
Resolution is the smallest distance at which two points still look separate.

16
00:01:08.697 --> 00:01:10.677
Magnification makes an image bigger.

17
00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:14.117
Resolution decides how much detail it holds.

18
00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:16.997
Many cells are almost clear.

19
00:01:17.837 --> 00:01:21.657
A stain is a dye that sticks to some cell parts more than others.

20
00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:23.117
It adds contrast.

21
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:29.430
The unaided eye separates details about 0.1 millimeters apart.

22
00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.790
That is enough for an African clawed frog egg.

23
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:37.990
An ordinary light microscope separates 0.2 micrometers.

24
00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.250
That is enough for a cheek cell or a bacterium.

25
00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:47.250
An electron microscope uses electrons, which have much shorter wavelengths than

26
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.270
visible light. It separates about 1 to 2 nanometers.

27
00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.870
That is enough for a ribosome.

28
00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:56.663
The theory also changed.

29
00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:01.043
Matthias Schleiden described plant tissues as made of cells.

30
00:02:01.923 --> 00:02:05.383
Theodor Schwann found the same cellular plan in animal tissues.

31
00:02:06.103 --> 00:02:10.463
But Schwann's model let new cells form inside a structureless fluid.

32
00:02:11.003 --> 00:02:12.003
That part was wrong.

33
00:02:12.903 --> 00:02:17.563
Robert Remak published evidence that new cells form when existing cells divide.

34
00:02:17.563 --> 00:02:22.603
Rudolf Virchow spread the idea: every cell comes from a cell.

35
00:02:23.383 --> 00:02:26.023
So why did it take better tools?

36
00:02:26.923 --> 00:02:32.043
A tool can show a structure only if its resolution is finer than the structure.

37
00:02:33.023 --> 00:02:35.483
Making the image bigger does not change that.

38
00:02:36.443 --> 00:02:40.283
The cell theory is a well-tested explanation, not a guess.

39
00:02:41.343 --> 00:02:44.003
Scientists corrected it as new evidence arrived.
